  <article class="report">
    <h1 class="page-title">How Pre-IPO Trades Actually Work &mdash; and Where Buyers Get Burned</h1>

    <p class="lede">Most of what&rsquo;s written about pre-IPO investing is written by people who have never closed a trade.</p>

    <p>This guide is different. It&rsquo;s a working broker&rsquo;s account of how private secondary transactions actually happen &mdash; the mechanics, the structures, the traps &mdash; drawn from ten years on the front lines of this market and nearly $200M in closed transactions, including SpaceX and Anthropic, two of the hardest names to actually deliver.</p>

    <h2>What&rsquo;s inside:</h2>

    <p><strong>The anatomy of a real trade.</strong> A closed transaction, walked through start to settlement: the indication, the pricing negotiation, the right-of-first-refusal clock, the documents, and how long each step really takes.</p>

    <p><strong>The many flavors of SPVs &mdash; and which to avoid.</strong> Not all vehicles are built alike. How to read a structure before you wire, and the ones that quietly eat your return.</p>

    <p><strong>Direct shares vs. SPVs.</strong> The real differences in what you own, and how experienced buyers position themselves to get directs.</p>

    <p><strong>What to know before trading through a platform.</strong> The economics behind &ldquo;free&rdquo; access, before you commit.</p>

    <p><strong>Red flags &mdash; and the questions that expose them.</strong> What phantom inventory looks like, what &ldquo;allocation&rdquo; claims actually mean, and the specific questions to put to any broker or seller before money moves.</p>

